  - name: HOUSEHOLDSURVEY_DICT.ICF_PART1
    conditions:
      - questionText:
          EN: |
            <p><img src="data:image/png;base64," width="512"/></p><p class="normal">We work for Asian Social Project Services, Inc. (ASPSI). We are here to ask you to participate in a study about the Universal Health Care (UHC) and packages of programs like Yaman ng Kalusugan Program (YAKAP), No Balance Billing (NBB), Zero Balance Billing (ZBB), Bagong Urgent Care and Ambulatory Services (BUCAS) center, and Guaranteed and Accessible Medications for Outpatient Treatment (GAMOT). The Department of Health funded this study. Please let me tell you more about the study.</p><p class="normal">This study aims to generate evidence on the overall experience of the general public to support continuous monitoring, evaluation, and learning of the implementation of the UHC Act and its Implementing Rules and Regulations (IRR). The questions will cover your household profiles, awareness and use of UHC programs like YAKAP/Konsulta, BUCAS, GAMOT, NBB, and ZBB, PhilHealth registration, health-seeking behaviors, primary care usage, referral experiences, and household expenditures.</p><p class="normal">Would you like to participate as a respondent in the study? The interview may last for more or less than an hour.</p><p class="instruction"><b>Universal Health Care (UHC) Survey-Year 2</b> &middot; Reference Year 2026</p><p class="instruction">PSA SSRCS Clearance No. DOH-2651-04 &middot; issued July 2026 &middot; valid until 31 July 2027<br/>SJREB: ICF ver. 07/25/2026 &middot; Translated Questionnaire ver. 06/05/2026</p>
          FIL: |
            <p><img src="data:image/png;base64," width="512"/></p><p class="normal">We work for Asian Social Project Services, Inc. (ASPSI). We are here to ask you to participate in a study about the Universal Health Care (UHC) and packages of programs like Yaman ng Kalusugan Program (YAKAP), No Balance Billing (NBB), Zero Balance Billing (ZBB), Bagong Urgent Care and Ambulatory Services (BUCAS) center, and Guaranteed and Accessible Medications for Outpatient Treatment (GAMOT). The Department of Health funded this study. Please let me tell you more about the study.</p><p class="normal">This study aims to generate evidence on the overall experience of the general public to support continuous monitoring, evaluation, and learning of the implementation of the UHC Act and its Implementing Rules and Regulations (IRR). The questions will cover your household profiles, awareness and use of UHC programs like YAKAP/Konsulta, BUCAS, GAMOT, NBB, and ZBB, PhilHealth registration, health-seeking behaviors, primary care usage, referral experiences, and household expenditures.</p><p class="normal">Would you like to participate as a respondent in the study? The interview may last for more or less than an hour.</p><p class="instruction"><b>Universal Health Care (UHC) Survey-Year 2</b> &middot; Reference Year 2026</p><p class="instruction">PSA SSRCS Clearance No. DOH-2651-04 &middot; issued July 2026 &middot; valid until 31 July 2027<br/>SJREB: ICF ver. 07/25/2026 &middot; Translated Questionnaire ver. 06/05/2026</p>
